  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two players, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, play a game against each other. In every round of the game, each player rolls a fair die once, where the six faces of the die have six distinct numbers. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math> denote the readings on the die rolled by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, respectively. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>y</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;scores <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;points and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;scores <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;point. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></math>, then each player scores&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> points. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>y</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;scores&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math> point and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;scores&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> points. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;be the total scores of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, respectively, after playing the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>i</mi><mi>th</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;round.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>List-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>List-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Probability of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8805;</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>II</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Probability of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>III</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Probability of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>IV</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Probability of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>355</mn><mn>864</mn></mfrac></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>77</mn><mn>432</mn></mfrac></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>The correct option is:</p>"
